  "text": "Round 5's elementwise kernel is kept unchanged, with one experiment: output stores now carry `eviction_policy=\"evict_last\"`. This change has not been measured yet.\n\n**Why the store hint:**\n- The kernel already moves 120 MiB of logical traffic in about 22.1 \u00b5s. That is roughly 87% of the measured 6.54 TB/s peak, and the remainder is mostly launch, ramp-up and tail overhead.\n- Rounds 2\u20136 changed tile shape, warps and scheduling, and all landed at 0.0221\u20130.0223 ms. Tiling is not the limit.\n- The only lever left is DRAM traffic during the kernel. The 40 MiB output fits easily in the 126.5 MiB L2.\n- Inputs are read once and marked `evict_first`, so they are the preferred victims. Outputs marked `evict_last` should stay resident as dirty lines, and their write-back can happen after the kernel instead of competing with the input reads.\n- If the L2 behaves as hoped, kernel-time DRAM traffic drops toward the 80 MiB of reads alone. If it does not, the hint should leave the runtime about where it is now.\n\nThe algorithm is unchanged: one launch, one pass, the add done in fp16, and the masked path handles any `n`.\n\n```python title=\"impl_triton.py\"\nimport torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Fixed configuration literals\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 128-thread CTAs, 32 fp16 per thread per tensor (4 x 16B vector accesses).\n# Inputs are streamed once (evict_first: preferred L2 victims); the output is\n# stored with evict_last so the 40 MiB of dirty output lines stay resident in\n# the 126.5 MiB L2 instead of competing with input reads for DRAM bandwidth\n# during the kernel (write-back is deferred until the lines are evicted).\n_BLOCK = 4096\n_NUM_WARPS = 4\n_NUM_STAGES = 1\n\n_CONFIG = {\n    \"BLOCK\": _BLOCK,\n    \"num_warps\": _NUM_WARPS,\n    \"num_stages\": _NUM_STAGES,\n    \"elems_per_thread\": _BLOCK // (_NUM_WARPS * 32),\n    \"load_eviction_policy\": \"evict_first\",\n    \"store_eviction_policy\": \"evict_last\",\n    \"store_cache_modifier\": \"default\",\n}\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _vector_add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n,\n                       BLOCK: tl.constexpr, EVEN: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(0)\n    offs = pid * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    offs = tl.max_contiguous(tl.multiple_of(offs, BLOCK), BLOCK)\n    if EVEN:\n        x = tl.load(x_ptr + offs, eviction_policy=\"evict_first\")\n        y = tl.load(y_ptr + offs, eviction_policy=\"evict_first\")\n        tl.store(out_ptr + offs, x + y, eviction_policy=\"evict_last\")\n    else:\n        mask = offs < n\n        x = tl.load(x_ptr + offs, mask=mask, other=0.0,\n                    eviction_policy=\"evict_first\")\n        y = tl.load(y_ptr + offs, mask=mask, other=0.0,\n                    eviction_policy=\"evict_first\")\n        tl.store(out_ptr + offs, x + y, mask=mask,\n                 eviction_policy=\"evict_last\")\n\n\ndef run(x, y):\n    x = x.contiguous()\n    y = y.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    grid = (triton.cdiv(n, _BLOCK),)\n    even = (n % _BLOCK) == 0\n    _vector_add_kernel[grid](\n        x, y, out, n,\n        BLOCK=_BLOCK, EVEN=even,\n        num_warps=_NUM_WARPS, num_stages=_NUM_STAGES,\n    )\n    return out\n\n\ndef get_last_config() -> dict:\n    return dict(_CONFIG)\n```",
